        <h2 id="privacy-content-heading" class="content-heading">1. Who We Are</h2>
        <p>This website is operated by Rutabanks Notary and Legal Services Ltd, a private company limited by shares registered in the Republic of Rwanda, based in Kigali. We are responsible for the personal data collected through this website.</p>

        <h2 class="content-heading">2. Information We Collect</h2>
        <p>We only collect personal data that you provide to us directly:</p>
        <ul>
          <li><strong>Contact form:</strong> your name, email address, phone number (optional), the service you are interested in and your message.</li>
          <li><strong>Appointment form:</strong> your full name, phone number, email address (optional), preferred date and time, the service required and any notes.</li>
        </ul>
        <p>We also keep the date and time of each submission. We do not use advertising or tracking cookies.</p>

        <h2 class="content-heading">3. How We Use Your Information</h2>
        <ul>
          <li>To respond to your enquiry;</li>
          <li>To schedule, confirm or reschedule your appointment;</li>
          <li>To contact you about the service you requested.</li>
        </ul>
        <p>We do not use your information for marketing and we never sell or rent it to anyone.</p>

        <h2 class="content-heading">4. Legal Basis</h2>
        <p>We process your personal data on the basis of the consent you give when you submit a form, in line with Law N° 058/2021 of 13/10/2021 relating to the protection of personal data and privacy in Rwanda. You may withdraw your consent at any time by contacting us.</p>

        <h2 class="content-heading">5. Sharing Your Information</h2>
        <p>Your information is only accessible to our firm. We use a trusted email provider to receive notifications about new messages and appointments. We will only disclose your information to others where required by law.</p>

        <h2 class="content-heading">6. How Long We Keep Your Information</h2>
        <p>Website enquiries and appointment requests are kept for up to 12 months after our last contact with you, unless a longer period is required for an ongoing service or by law. After that they are deleted.</p>

        <h2 class="content-heading">7. Security</h2>
        <p>We take reasonable technical and organisational measures to protect your data, including restricting access to authorised staff and protecting our administration area with a password. However, no method of transmission over the internet is completely secure, so please do not send highly sensitive documents through the website forms.</p>

        <h2 class="content-heading">8. Your Rights</h2>
        <p>You have the right to:</p>
        <ul>
          <li>Ask for a copy of the personal data we hold about you;</li>
          <li>Ask us to correct inaccurate information;</li>
          <li>Ask us to delete your information;</li>
          <li>Withdraw your consent at any time;</li>
          <li>Lodge a complaint with the National Cyber Security Authority (NCSA), the supervisory authority for personal data protection in Rwanda.</li>
        </ul>

        <h2 class="content-heading">9. Contact Us About Your Data</h2>
